1. LICENCE MAP

1.1 MIT front-end code

The MIT Licence in Appendix A applies to:

- source code under `src/client/`;
- generic browser-interface markup, styling and client-side support code under
  `public/`; and
- any other file that expressly states that it is licensed under the MIT
  Licence or carries `SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`.

The MIT Licence applies only to code. It does not apply to the engine,
characters, personas, artwork, images, narrative material, prompts, reader
identities, branding or other protected material described below, even when
such material is stored in, referenced by, or embedded alongside MIT-licensed
front-end code.

1.2 Proprietary source-available engine

The Online Arcana engine is proprietary source-available software. It includes:

- source code under `src/core/`;
- server-side and API code under `functions/`;
- prompt construction, response orchestration and model-integration logic;
- reading, spread, suitability, referral, handover, synthesis, archive and
  conversation logic; and
- any other file that expressly states that it is governed by the Online
  Arcana Engine Terms in section 2 or carries
  `SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Online-Arcana-Engine`.

Where engine logic exists elsewhere under `src/`, section 2 applies to that
logic. The express MIT grant for `src/client/` takes precedence for ordinary,
generic front-end code in that directory, subject to the protected-content
exceptions in section 1.3.

1.3 Protected creative material and identity

All original creative material and intellectual identity associated with
Online Arcana are copyright protected and all rights are reserved. This
includes, without limitation:

- characters, readers, names, personas, personalities, biographies, dialogue,
  voices, relationships and lore;
- reader instructions, persona prompts and characteristic response material;
- illustrations, photographs, card artwork, symbols, emblems, logos, icons,
  visual compositions and animations;
- distinctive themes, palettes, presentation, written copy and narrative
  expression; and
- the Online Arcana name, identity and branding.

These protections apply regardless of the file or directory containing the
material. Nothing in this licence claims exclusive rights in traditional tarot
concepts, public-domain material, standard card names, general ideas or
uncopyrightable facts. The protection applies to Online Arcana's original
expression and identity.

If a file contains both licensed code and protected creative material, the
applicable code licence does not grant permission to copy, adapt, extract or
reuse the protected creative material.

2. ONLINE ARCANA ENGINE TERMS

2.1 Source inspection grant

Subject to these terms, you may:

- access, read and study the engine source code;
- make and retain exact, unmodified copies of the engine solely for inspection,
  archival, backup and preservation purposes;
- run the original engine as distributed for personal evaluation, testing and
  security review; and
- describe its externally observable behaviour and general ideas in your own
  words.

Every permitted copy must retain this licence and all copyright, attribution
and proprietary notices.

2.2 Restrictions

Except with prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

- copy or reuse engine source code, in whole or in substantial part, in another
  work;
- modify, adapt, arrange, translate, transpile or create a derivative work from
  the engine source code;
- publish, distribute or maintain a modified version or fork of the engine;
- incorporate engine source code or protected implementation structure into
  another programme, library, service or product;
- remove or alter copyright, attribution, licence or proprietary notices;
- sublicense, sell, rent or commercially exploit the engine source code; or
- use the engine source code as training data or input for a system intended to
  reproduce, transform or generate the same or substantially similar protected
  implementation.

An exact, unmodified archival or preservation copy permitted by section 2.1 is
not a fork. A repository or distribution containing changes to the engine is a
fork or derivative work and is not permitted.

2.3 Independent implementation is permitted

You may independently implement the ideas, algorithms, interfaces, file
formats and externally observable behaviour of the engine, provided that the
new implementation is genuinely independently written and does not copy,
adapt, translate or derive from protected expression in the engine source
code.

Equivalent functionality or behaviour alone does not breach these terms.
Permission under this section does not include permission to use the protected
characters, personas, artwork, identity or other material described in section
1.3.

2.4 No implied rights

Possession of, access to, or visibility of the engine source code grants no
rights beyond those expressly stated here. All other rights are reserved.

3. CREATIVE MATERIAL TERMS

The material described in section 1.3 may be included only when making or
running an exact, unmodified copy of Online Arcana as permitted by this
licence. It may not be extracted, republished, adapted, imitated, incorporated
into another work, used to create derivative characters or personas, or used
separately from the unmodified software without prior written permission.

No right is granted to use the Online Arcana name, logos, reader identities or
other branding in a way that suggests affiliation, endorsement or authorship.

4. TERMINATION

Any permission granted under sections 2 or 3 terminates automatically upon a
breach of these terms. On termination, all unauthorised copies and derivative
materials must be destroyed, without limiting any other rights or remedies of
the copyright holder.

